    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21-a1">

                <pb facs="0086" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg12"/>

                <head>Mr. Stanton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 8, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to your letter of the 14th
                    ultimo, enclosing a copy of a communication from Lord Lyons relative to some
                    shot fired from a battery in course of construction on an island near Eastport,
                    Maine, having fallen upon the British territory at Campobello, I have the honor
                    to transmit, herewith, copies of papers submitted to this department by Major
                    General Dix, commanding the department of the east, who was directed to
                    investigate the subject and take proper measures to prevent a repetition of the
                    alleged offence.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWIN M. STANTON, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        War.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>







